      "last_reviewed": "2026-07-28",
      "notes": "Source availability (T5.4): open -- the repository carries 90 HDL source files (82 systemverilog, 5 verilog, 3 vhdl) alongside 9 prebuilt .rbf binaries. There is no open_source column in the delivered schema (data-model.md §1.9 deleted the proposed core table together with its flags); the presence of hdl_language_id and of implementation_path rows is how that fact is stated here. Machine mapping: hand-mapped, not MRA-setname-derived -- a console core ships no MRA files. The core reimplements the Sega Saturn, giving machine_id saturn. Every id was checked against extract/machine.json. This console core doubles as an arcade core: Machine mapping: 43 arcade MRA files in Distribution_MiSTer/_Arcade naming <rbf>ST-V</rbf> carry a <setname>; 43 resolved exactly to a MAME 0.288 machine and 0 through MAME's own cloneof relation to the parent set that survives extract/machine.json's parents-only filter, giving 43 distinct machine_id rows. Those setnames are MAME shortnames, so this part of the mapping is setname-derived. License: the repository has no LICENSE, COPYING or COPYRIGHT file; the grant lives in the source header at https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Saturn_MiSTer/blob/main/Saturn.sv, which offers the work under the GNU General Public License \"either version 2 of the License, or (at your option) any later version\" -- hence GPL-2.0-or-later. hdl_language_id: 82 of 90 HDL files are systemverilog (82 systemverilog, 5 verilog, 3 vhdl), excluding the shared framework directory. accuracy_id omitted: the repository makes no timing-fidelity claim this build could verify."
    }
  ],
